      "source_id": "39f5d2a7-fc13-4e5a-875b-df5111242952",
      "text": "For heatwaves, the main thing to keep in mind is providing constant hydration and shade. You'll want to ensure your plants are getting enough water, and if possible, move any sensitive plants to a shaded or more sheltered spot. You might also want to consider using some kind of evaporative cooling if you can, like misting or using a fan to create a breeze, which can help regulate the air around them without letting them get too hot."
    },
    {
      "available": true,
      "role": "external",
      "slot": "s4",
      "source_id": "5246afa7-c7ec-4709-bc9d-37bd03809a7a",
      "text": "I'll make sure to keep an eye on the watering schedule and maybe set up some shade for the more delicate ones. Thanks for the advice, it's good to have a plan."
    },
    {
      "available": true,
      "role": "model_output",
      "slot": "s5",
      "source_id": "d4723cb8-520f-4381-ae9f-823112625f37",
      "text": "You're very welcome! Just remember that consistency is key—regular checks will give you the most accurate data. Let me know if you have any other questions as you start this new routine!"
    }
